WEBVTT

00:03.135 --> 00:06.012
O-Ow! It's here…

00:06.138 --> 00:09.307
Hey, Fugo… Look and tell me
what you think, okay?

00:09.392 --> 00:12.144
Whoa, you really did
a number on yourself.

00:12.228 --> 00:13.437
You got a real goose egg there.

00:13.521 --> 00:15.231
Ow! That hurts!

00:15.273 --> 00:18.359
Knock it off, will ya?!
Don't touch it!

00:20.820 --> 00:23.030
Pezzo di merda!

00:23.072 --> 00:25.240
You're gonna suffer for
what you did, you bastard!

00:25.283 --> 00:27.618
I've got this fat knob on my skull
because of your dumb ass!

00:27.660 --> 00:30.162
I hope you're ready!

00:30.246 --> 00:32.331
Take this! And this!

00:32.415 --> 00:34.750
Cazzo! You really thought you were
better than us, shit head?!

00:34.792 --> 00:36.293
You ball-less, mother…!

00:47.471 --> 00:49.306
Hey, something fell off him.

00:49.932 --> 00:51.308
Let's see…

00:51.684 --> 00:54.520
Mario Zucchero.
Says he lives in Rome.

00:54.604 --> 00:56.772
So he's a Roman hooligan.

01:04.363 --> 01:07.657
That thing stuck to your face…
looks like a piece of trash.

01:07.742 --> 01:10.411
Or maybe it's a piece of seaweed.

01:10.953 --> 01:13.163
It looks like a piece of seaweed,

01:13.205 --> 01:16.416
but it could also easily be
a piece of plastic.

01:18.210 --> 01:21.171
It pains my soul to think
that could be trash.

01:21.213 --> 01:24.507
'Cause that'd mean
these wondrous waters are polluted.

01:24.675 --> 01:27.719
You don't mind if
I inspect the specimen, do you?

01:28.429 --> 01:29.930
Hey.

01:30.806 --> 01:33.892
I asked if I could take a closer look
at that thing on your face.

01:34.143 --> 01:38.188
At least have the decency
to answer me that.

01:41.108 --> 01:42.192
<i>Capri.</i>

01:42.652 --> 01:47.152
<i>Long ago, when the ancient Greeks
colonized the Mediterranean,</i>

01:47.657 --> 01:52.157
<i>explorers sought out the most
stunning landscapes in the land.</i>

01:52.328 --> 01:53.245
<i>On discovering the isle of Capri,</i>

01:53.329 --> 01:54.955
<i>they knew they had found
their destination.</i>

01:55.373 --> 01:57.875
<i>Blessed with azure waters
and brilliant skies,</i>

01:57.917 --> 02:00.294
<i>Capri flaunts
her steep ivory precipices…</i>

02:00.336 --> 02:04.757
<i>the cliffs soaring from the sea below
like a single grand fortress.</i>

02:04.840 --> 02:06.716
<i>During the age of the Roman Empire,</i>

02:06.801 --> 02:09.553
<i>one emperor decided to construct
several villas on the island,</i>

02:09.637 --> 02:11.889
<i>where he remained
until his death ten years later.</i>

02:12.056 --> 02:14.224
<i>Now, before Bruno Bucciarati
and his crew</i>

02:14.266 --> 02:18.766
<i>a mystifying island conceals
a dazzling fortune worth ten billion lira.</i>

02:34.537 --> 02:39.037
<i>Heavy stones of fate
are holding down my dreams</i>

02:39.875 --> 02:43.336
<i>It feels as if I'm being crushed</i>

02:45.089 --> 02:49.589
<i>I've been staggering around
with nowhere to hide</i>

02:50.261 --> 02:54.098
<i>But I will never give in</i>

02:54.181 --> 02:58.681
<i>I know there are fragments of hope
buried beneath all that rubble</i>

03:05.943 --> 03:10.443
<i>I will find them with my own hands
and turn this world upside down</i>

03:19.040 --> 03:23.540
<i>Fighting gold
We will shine one day</i>

03:25.004 --> 03:29.504
<i>As long as we continue to
believe in our own path</i>

03:32.094 --> 03:35.222
<i>We are unyielding souls</i>

03:35.264 --> 03:39.764
<i>Our battle against god
will keep raging on</i>

03:40.519 --> 03:45.019
<i>Until our final days
Fighting gold</i>

03:54.825 --> 03:59.325
EPISODE 07
SIX BULLETS APPEARS, PART 1

03:57.286 --> 03:59.601
Bucciarati, we should map out
our route to the island.

04:01.540 --> 04:03.583
I've been on the look out
for a while now,

04:04.210 --> 04:06.420
I haven't spotted a single boat
trying to tail us.

04:06.462 --> 04:10.424
There's no way anyone would know
this boat is heading to the island of Capri.

04:10.800 --> 04:13.511
Yes, we're clear of boats, but…

04:13.552 --> 04:16.930
what I want to know is who told
that bastard about the secret fortune.

04:17.431 --> 04:21.226
I don't believe for a second that
he followed us here alone.

04:23.312 --> 04:26.815
You know, I noticed you've been
eyeing these things for a while now.

04:26.857 --> 04:28.859
Well, they're not mine.

04:28.943 --> 04:30.986
They were inside the boat.

04:32.488 --> 04:34.740
Which would you like me to use?

04:34.782 --> 04:36.742
The glasses or the fishing line?

04:36.826 --> 04:40.371
If we don't get some answers from you,
it's not going to be pretty.

04:40.454 --> 04:44.040
Your answers are going to help
keep us out of danger.

04:44.166 --> 04:46.960
You don't work alone,
do you, Mr. Zucchero?

04:47.002 --> 04:50.088
And I'm gonna take a wild guess
and say he is a Stand user, am I right?

04:50.881 --> 04:52.924
That's why I'll be using these.

04:53.008 --> 04:54.384
You can't even tell me

04:54.426 --> 04:56.386
which of these beauties
you want me to use, eh?

04:56.512 --> 04:58.764
If you can't decide…

05:00.015 --> 05:04.227
I'll just have to use both!

05:08.816 --> 05:11.902
How's that?
Feel like chatting now?

05:11.944 --> 05:16.444
Ma-ri-o Zuc-che-ro.
Heaven, Hell, Purgatory…

05:17.032 --> 05:18.616
Heaven, Hell, or…

05:19.201 --> 05:20.577
Purgatory!

05:22.538 --> 05:25.582
Ha, looks like he lucked out!
You, my man, get to go to Purgatory!

06:15.424 --> 06:17.551
If you're not gonna
fess up about

06:17.593 --> 06:21.305
the powers and name of
your stalker friend hot on our trail…

06:21.388 --> 06:24.015
You might want to start worrying

06:24.099 --> 06:28.144
about the well being of
your good eye, Mr. Zucchero!

06:28.229 --> 06:30.481
How long were you planning
on dick in' around, coglioni?

06:30.940 --> 06:33.734
Idiots, come here and look at this.

06:33.776 --> 06:36.153
Bastard, he was using
the radio on the boat.

06:36.237 --> 06:39.281
So you stumbled across something
with Moody Jazz's replay.

06:39.865 --> 06:40.824
Let's see what he found.

06:41.450 --> 06:44.202
This boat may've been flatter
than a pizza

06:44.245 --> 06:46.830
but it's back to normal now
and so is our culprit.

06:54.546 --> 06:55.463
Giorno!

06:55.923 --> 06:58.717
You're not going to see my Stand!

06:58.759 --> 06:59.926
Turn around.

07:00.010 --> 07:02.971
It's your lucky day.
I'll let you hear his voice.

07:05.683 --> 07:10.183
His replay clearly shows him using
the radio in the cabin below.

07:10.521 --> 07:11.897
He's contacting someone.

07:12.564 --> 07:15.024
I already got four of 'em hostage.

07:15.109 --> 07:17.611
I just need to nab Bucciarati
and that other guy.

07:17.778 --> 07:19.654
I'll be done here in no time.

07:19.738 --> 07:21.614
I know their destination…

07:21.657 --> 07:23.033
Capri!

07:24.034 --> 07:26.745
- They haven't come out…
- Now what do we do?

07:26.829 --> 07:28.539
- With anything specific yet.
- He heard absolutely everything!

07:28.789 --> 07:30.916
Once I dispose of
his little bootlickers,

07:31.000 --> 07:33.877
I'll get Bucciarati to cough up
the money spot. Over.

07:34.461 --> 07:37.630
<i>Was that yacht named</i> Lagoon?

07:37.881 --> 07:39.549
<i>Identify your whereabouts.</i>

07:39.591 --> 07:42.844
We're no more than two hours from
landing on the island of Capri.

07:43.262 --> 07:47.762
Bucciarati is trying to lose any pursuers
by taking a roundabout way.

07:49.518 --> 07:50.852
<i>Understood</i>

07:50.853 --> 07:53.564
<i>I'll take a speedboat to Capri
and meet you there.</i>

07:53.564 --> 07:56.900
<i>Dock at Marina Grande.
Over and out.</i>

07:59.862 --> 08:02.865
That's as far as it goes.
The radio just cuts out.

08:03.365 --> 08:04.532
Well, that's just perfect.

08:04.575 --> 08:06.493
We're screwed. That speedboat

08:06.618 --> 08:08.703
is going to zip him from Napoli to Capri
in less than thirty minutes!

08:09.371 --> 08:11.915
That's it…
He's already on the island!

08:11.957 --> 08:15.418
Who was that? Who the hell was
that guy on the other end?

08:15.544 --> 08:16.753
Fine, no more games…

08:16.795 --> 08:20.590
This flesh bag is gonna tell us,
and he's gonna tell us now!

08:20.883 --> 08:24.094
No, he's a die-hard mafioso.

08:24.261 --> 08:27.097
Getting him to come clean
is going to take some time.

08:27.139 --> 08:29.558
I doubt he'll tell us
anything today.

08:29.600 --> 08:33.312
Besides, we can't assume he even knows
anything about his partner's Stand.

08:33.729 --> 08:36.648
It's very likely he kept it
a complete secret, even to him.

08:36.732 --> 08:38.275
Then where's that leave us?

08:38.359 --> 08:40.527
What are we waiting for?
Let's just head to the harbor.

08:40.694 --> 08:44.906
If he finds out Zucchero isn't
the only one on this boat…

08:44.948 --> 08:49.448
If this boat doesn't arrive at
Marina Grande in an hour's time…

08:50.329 --> 08:54.624
That guy on the radio will have to think
something happened to Zucchero.

08:54.708 --> 08:57.794
If that happens,
you can kiss that fortune good bye.

08:57.878 --> 08:58.670
No…

08:58.754 --> 09:02.299
We'll be lucky to make it back
to Napoli alive!

09:04.301 --> 09:06.803
What'll it be, Bucciarati?

09:10.182 --> 09:12.100
<i>Indecision is not an option.</i>

09:12.226 --> 09:15.312
<i>We have to take action
and outsmart.</i>

09:15.396 --> 09:17.147
<i>Somehow, I will make it
to that island first…</i>

09:17.189 --> 09:18.982
Before this boat docks…

09:23.529 --> 09:28.029
…someone needs to preemptively locate
and take down the man on the island.

09:30.702 --> 09:32.829
What the hell kind of crazy shit
is this guy saying?

09:32.871 --> 09:35.665
Are you a freakin' idiot?

09:35.707 --> 09:38.167
Someone's supposed to get to
the island before this boat?

09:38.210 --> 09:40.420
What, you want one of us
to swim there?

09:40.421 --> 09:41.171
Yes.

09:41.171 --> 09:41.921
Huh?!

09:42.506 --> 09:45.258
I'll transform this buoy
into a fish.

09:45.384 --> 09:49.763
It can pull me faster than
this boat can sail.

09:50.722 --> 09:53.683
Don't worry, it's my Stand,
so I designate myself to go.

09:57.187 --> 09:59.522
I refuse to let anything or anyone
get in the way of my dream.

10:00.065 --> 10:02.192
I want that ten billion lira.

10:02.234 --> 10:05.111
We'll use it to make
Bucciarati capo.

10:06.864 --> 10:09.950
We'll use it to work our way up
through the famiglia.

10:10.159 --> 10:11.326
Giorno…

10:17.666 --> 10:20.418
You want to go?
Fine, knock yourself out.

10:20.669 --> 10:23.088
You dream up some
pretty clever ideas, boy.

10:23.172 --> 10:25.465
But it's too bad
you don't have a freakin' clue

10:25.507 --> 10:27.258
as to what he looks like
or what he's called.

10:27.968 --> 10:30.553
The port of Capri is crawling
with tourists.

10:30.679 --> 10:33.431
How in the hell do you think
you're gonna find him?

10:33.515 --> 10:36.142
I'm with Giorno on this one.

10:37.060 --> 10:39.771
So what if we don't know
who this asshole is?

10:39.897 --> 10:44.397
If he's waiting for Zucchero
to arrive in this boat,

10:45.444 --> 10:47.571
I think we've got
a fighting chance.

10:47.821 --> 10:50.156
Why wait for him to make his move?

10:52.534 --> 10:54.327
The bastard won't know
what hit him.

10:56.663 --> 10:58.247
So, about that fish…

10:58.290 --> 11:00.875
How many people you think
it can drag along, Giorno?

11:03.045 --> 11:07.007
My Stand, Six Bullets,
is designed to kill.

11:10.886 --> 11:13.430
They'll be more than happy
to oblige.

11:14.890 --> 11:16.349
We'll keep you company.

11:20.646 --> 11:22.606
GUIDO MISTA
SIX BULLETS

11:33.825 --> 11:37.787
Swimming from that yacht took
a bit longer than I expected.

11:38.163 --> 11:40.123
We have twenty minutes before

11:40.165 --> 11:42.792
Zucchero is supposed to meet
with our man of mystery.

11:42.918 --> 11:45.253
We don't have much more time
than that.

11:45.254 --> 11:47.631
Giorno, how does the marina look?

11:49.299 --> 11:51.134
Well, not the greatest.

11:51.176 --> 11:55.676
Abbacchio wasn't kidding,
Tourists are everywhere.

11:55.931 --> 11:57.891
Everyone seems to be waiting
for somebody else.

11:58.475 --> 12:02.645
Of course, most of them are waiting
for arriving ships, but…

12:03.188 --> 12:06.566
Signore Mista,
You <i>do</i> have a plan

12:06.608 --> 12:10.194
to weed out this guy from the masses
in the next 20 minutes, right?

12:24.543 --> 12:26.419
What… are you doing?

12:29.881 --> 12:32.925
If you were paying attention,
you'd you know it's long past lunchtime.

12:33.010 --> 12:36.430
What I'd really like to do is go
to that restaurant there,

12:36.471 --> 12:39.265
but everyone knows the restaurants
right on the water

12:39.308 --> 12:41.018
serve that shitty touristy crap.

12:41.059 --> 12:43.603
I don't have a clue about
what this guy looks like,

12:43.645 --> 12:46.022
but I'm guessing he wouldn't say
the same about me.

12:46.106 --> 12:48.399
I am on Bucciarati's team.

12:48.483 --> 12:50.401
He probably knows
what you look like too.

12:51.737 --> 12:54.531
I have to apologize,
but I'm not following at all.

12:54.781 --> 12:56.407
If I may, Mista…

12:56.450 --> 12:58.535
I know we were talking about
having twenty minutes left

12:58.577 --> 13:01.663
but even if he's just a little bit of a worrier,
we probably have only ten.

13:01.705 --> 13:03.039
It could be even more like five.

13:03.206 --> 13:06.042
He may get suspicious when
the <i>Lagoon</i> fails to arrive

13:06.043 --> 13:09.129
and catch on that
something's happened to Zucchero.

13:09.588 --> 13:11.965
If that happens,
our man will be untraceable.

13:12.007 --> 13:13.299
We can't waste another minute ju—

13:13.342 --> 13:15.385
And I told you,
I'm on my lunch break!

13:15.510 --> 13:17.803
Lunchtime is when you eat lunch!

13:17.971 --> 13:21.182
Go to any boutique or bookstore in
this country and you will find out.

13:21.391 --> 13:24.268
No one can work on
an empty stomach.

13:25.187 --> 13:28.064
Hey, I'm not like that.

13:28.523 --> 13:32.235
But these fellas take
the custom pretty seriously.

13:34.029 --> 13:35.363
Lunchtime!

13:35.364 --> 13:36.365
Give us something yummy!

13:36.365 --> 13:39.659
Here, ragazzi,
here are some num nums.

13:39.701 --> 13:41.828
Salame toscano e buono!

13:45.123 --> 13:45.957
Yummy!

13:46.166 --> 13:47.292
The best!

13:47.334 --> 13:49.419
Hey, gimme that!

13:50.545 --> 13:53.172
Hey, knock it off, Number 3!

13:53.215 --> 13:55.759
Stop making Number 5 cry!

13:55.801 --> 13:58.512
Enough bickering.
There's plenty for everyone.

13:58.845 --> 14:01.514
Each one thinks
he works the hardest,

14:01.556 --> 14:04.850
so each one thinks
he deserves the most food.

14:04.893 --> 14:07.812
I always make sure
no one gets left out.

14:11.316 --> 14:14.569
Number 5, at some point
you have to stop crying!

14:15.070 --> 14:17.113
What are they, exactly?

14:17.114 --> 14:18.949
How many of those things
do you have?

14:19.032 --> 14:21.451
Hey, don't call them "things."

14:21.451 --> 14:23.953
They really don't like it when
you treat them like pets.

14:24.079 --> 14:25.455
There are six of them.

14:25.455 --> 14:29.125
You won't see a Number 4 here,
it's bad luck.

14:29.167 --> 14:32.170
There's one for each bullet.

14:32.462 --> 14:33.796
For each bullet?

14:33.839 --> 14:37.217
This guy wants us to hurry up.

14:37.300 --> 14:41.762
It sure would be nice if you guys could
take your nap after you finish the job.

14:41.763 --> 14:44.223
Forget it!

14:44.808 --> 14:46.684
Hey, Number 3!

14:46.727 --> 14:49.062
I told you, stop hitting!

14:49.104 --> 14:49.854
Mista!

14:49.938 --> 14:52.273
I'll try and persuade them.

14:52.774 --> 14:53.649
So, Giorno…

14:54.067 --> 14:57.153
You can get the radio
out of the bag.

15:07.622 --> 15:09.665
Once work's done,
it's gobble time!

15:09.708 --> 15:11.376
It's balls to the wall, guys!

15:18.300 --> 15:21.386
Pay attention. I'm gonna make
my way to the guard shack

15:21.470 --> 15:24.848
and use the building's shadows to
conceal myself from peering eyes.

15:28.935 --> 15:32.855
Calling all passengers of
the <i>Lagoon…</i>

15:33.315 --> 15:37.815
We have a message
from Signore Zucchero!

15:38.862 --> 15:42.031
Please make your way
to the guard shack!

15:42.157 --> 15:46.286
Calling all passengers of
the <i>Lagoon.</i>

15:46.369 --> 15:50.498
We have a message
from Signore Zucchero!

15:50.540 --> 15:52.583
- Please come to the guard shack!
<i>- So he's playing it safe and pretending</i>

15:52.584 --> 15:54.752
- Please come to the guard shack!
<i>- he didn't hear the announcement…</i>

15:54.836 --> 15:58.714
<i>Or he thinks it's a sign they've figured out
where the loot's been hidden</i>

15:58.799 --> 16:00.717
<i>and he's about to jump out and celebrate
for being ten billion lira richer.</i>

16:00.759 --> 16:02.218
<i>It's all a gamble.</i>

16:02.302 --> 16:05.388
- Calling all passengers of the <i>Lagoon.
- Whoever hears the announcement</i>

16:05.388 --> 16:06.597
- Calling all passengers of the <i>Lagoon.
- and heads to the guards hack.</i>

16:06.640 --> 16:08.850
- We have a message from Signore Zucchero!
<i>- for the message is our mystery man.</i>

16:08.850 --> 16:10.059
- We have a message from Signore Zucchero!
<i>- Giorno, if anyone goes anywhere</i>

16:10.143 --> 16:14.643
- Please come to the guard shack!
<i>- near the guards hack, give me a sign.</i>

16:15.190 --> 16:18.735
<i>Whoever answers that call
is gonna get a head full of lead!</i>

16:19.027 --> 16:22.280
<i>Then again, Bucciarati wants
that ass alive,</i>

16:22.364 --> 16:24.699
<i>so I guess I should avoid
his important parts.</i>

16:24.699 --> 16:26.075
<i>That means we'll do our best.</i>

16:26.576 --> 16:28.995
<i>No one wants to make a move…</i>

16:29.371 --> 16:31.164
<i>No one's heading over there.</i>

16:31.206 --> 16:34.375
Attenzione, this is the last call…

16:34.417 --> 16:37.128
Calling all passengers
of the <i>Lagoon.</i>

16:37.629 --> 16:41.299
We have a message
from Signore Zucchero!

16:45.971 --> 16:48.431
<i>Merda, no one.
Nothing's happening.</i>

16:48.431 --> 16:51.100
<i>He's gotta be somewhere
on this island.</i>

16:51.142 --> 16:53.602
<i>Could he really be playing it safe
and refusing to appear?</i>

16:54.229 --> 16:56.689
<i>Did something happen, Zucchero?</i>

16:58.233 --> 17:00.026
<i>Why did you request
an announcement?</i>

17:00.068 --> 17:02.904
<i>Is there a problem? Over.</i>

17:07.075 --> 17:08.493
What's going on?

17:08.577 --> 17:11.079
No one's showing up at that
damn lookout shack.

17:15.584 --> 17:17.294
He's there! How?!

17:17.335 --> 17:20.796
I just don't… That lookout…
It must have another entrance.

17:20.881 --> 17:23.592
Shit, he's already inside!

17:24.301 --> 17:26.136
<i>It's too dark,
I can't see his face.</i>

17:26.219 --> 17:28.012
<i>Mista doesn't have a clue!</i>

17:28.430 --> 17:32.434
<i>If things don't turn around,
this guy is going to catch on and run!</i>

17:32.976 --> 17:34.477
<i>I have to let Mista know!</i>

17:38.481 --> 17:41.775
<i>What? The guy from the radio
is coming here now?</i>

17:45.989 --> 17:47.156
<i>Which one is it?</i>

17:47.532 --> 17:50.284
<i>Who's coming to the lookout shack?</i>

17:52.454 --> 17:53.872
<i>N-No!</i>

17:53.914 --> 17:55.874
<i>No one's going to the lookout!</i>

17:56.124 --> 17:57.959
<i>He's already inside!</i>

17:57.959 --> 17:59.335
<i>Just stay where you are!</i>

18:00.795 --> 18:02.505
He's by the window!

18:12.265 --> 18:14.433
<i>That bastard is…
There's no question…</i>

18:14.476 --> 18:16.394
<i>he's with Bucciarati!</i>

18:16.478 --> 18:19.814
<i>Zucchero was supposed to
get rid of him on that boat.</i>

18:19.981 --> 18:22.024
Mista! Behind you!

18:22.025 --> 18:24.944
He's on the radio! Mista!

18:25.195 --> 18:26.905
Damn it! He can't hear me.

18:27.489 --> 18:29.699
It's better than him not noticing!

18:29.741 --> 18:30.783
He's already there!

18:31.201 --> 18:34.537
<i>Mista! He's already on the radio!</i>

18:48.802 --> 18:51.429
Come on! Pass, pass, pass!

18:52.514 --> 18:54.766
Go, Six Bullets!

18:56.810 --> 18:58.520
MENACING

18:56.935 --> 18:58.478
Here we go!

19:05.777 --> 19:07.695
Shoot!

19:08.989 --> 19:10.490
BAZOO

19:16.454 --> 19:18.038
Yay!

19:18.081 --> 19:19.290
Boo yah!

19:19.374 --> 19:21.876
Yeah! Yeah! Yeah! Yeah!

19:22.877 --> 19:24.420
D-Did he get him?

19:27.257 --> 19:29.342
Wh-Who the hell are you?!

19:29.384 --> 19:30.843
W-What was that noise?

19:30.885 --> 19:32.303
Gunshots.

19:32.387 --> 19:34.347
Oh, I'm sorry, did I disturb you?

19:34.389 --> 19:37.892
'Cause I'm pretty sure it wasn't nearly
as bad as anything in the movies.

19:38.393 --> 19:41.521
Now if it truly did
disturb you, good sir…

19:41.563 --> 19:44.065
I'm kinda in the middle of things,

19:44.065 --> 19:46.734
but I assure you I will be available later
to address all complaints.

19:49.237 --> 19:51.322
Giorno's always in a hurry.

19:54.951 --> 19:57.119
So there was a rear entrance…

19:57.162 --> 20:00.957
He must have come in through this door
and got on the radio that way.

20:01.249 --> 20:04.627
Either he's being super careful
or the bastard has the weird habit

20:04.669 --> 20:08.547
of always trying to enter buildings
on the down low.

20:08.882 --> 20:09.966
Either way…

20:10.425 --> 20:12.427
- Excellent work, Bullets!
- Yay!

20:12.427 --> 20:13.594
The leg!

20:13.595 --> 20:16.097
- The leg! Hey, hey!
- We got his right leg!

20:16.097 --> 20:18.599
We got his right leg good!

20:18.600 --> 20:21.311
Yeah, you sure nailed that sucker.

20:21.352 --> 20:22.644
He's not going anywhere!

20:29.194 --> 20:31.696
Out front,
I've got the usual tourists…

20:31.738 --> 20:33.823
And back here is a freakin' cliff.

20:33.907 --> 20:35.742
No way he could climb that thing.

20:35.909 --> 20:37.994
He must be stumbling
around here somewhere.

20:37.994 --> 20:40.079
Now where would he be hiding…?

20:49.089 --> 20:50.965
He must be in that truck.

20:51.007 --> 20:55.507
<i>If he's a Stand user,
then he's a close-range one with power.</i>

20:57.847 --> 21:02.347
<i>If he were the long-range type,
he would've attacked me a long time ago.</i>

21:03.311 --> 21:07.523
<i>What that means is that,
this guy's got a bum leg.</i>

21:07.565 --> 21:09.358
<i>So he's probably hiding
behind this truck.</i>

21:09.400 --> 21:13.654
<i>Which means he's trying
to lure me in for the kill.</i>

21:13.905 --> 21:18.034
<i>Well, it's not like he could get me
even if I did get close.</i>

21:19.786 --> 21:22.371
<i>He's probably just beyond there.</i>

21:22.413 --> 21:26.291
<i>But I still don't have a freakin' clue
what his Stand can do.</i>

21:26.334 --> 21:29.211
<i>Going in without backup would
be risky to say the least.</i>

21:29.337 --> 21:30.880
<i>I should wait for Giorno and—</i>

21:32.674 --> 21:35.301
<i>Well, I guess that option's out.</i>

21:35.343 --> 21:37.219
<i>So the cazzo's in
the drivers eat now.</i>

21:37.220 --> 21:39.347
<i>He must've jump-started
the engine.</i>

21:39.389 --> 21:42.183
<i>I can't let him getaway now,
especially here.</i>

21:43.226 --> 21:44.602
Damn it! Dio cane!

21:44.727 --> 21:46.937
I still don't know what
this asshole looks like!

21:47.021 --> 21:48.480
I know Giorno doesn't either!

21:48.523 --> 21:51.359
Well, this guy's Stand is going to
have to remain a mystery for now!

21:51.401 --> 21:53.486
This is for the ten billion
and Bucciarati!

21:59.617 --> 22:00.826
Mangia merda!

22:04.539 --> 22:05.414
Mista!

23:37.966 --> 23:42.095
EPISODE 08
SIX BULLETS APPEARS, PART 2
